# Audit — 2026-09-22

Scope: full audit of `job_access_assist` as of branch `feat/milestone1-34`
(code for milestones 1–44), with **no Android device, emulator or live
OpenAI key available**. Every finding below comes from reading source,
plugin package sources in the pub cache, `flutter analyze`, `flutter test`,
and `flutter devices`. Anything that cannot be settled that way is marked
**Cannot verify without device** / **Cannot verify without API key** —
those are not guesses dressed up as results.

Legend — **Status**: Confirmed working / Confirmed broken / Cannot verify
without device / Cannot verify without API key.

Section 1.8 (added during the audit) lists real-target problems found that
were not in the brief. Section 2 records what Phase 2 changed, and section 3
is the "safe to assume vs. still unverified" summary.

---

## 1.1 Platform-mismatch hypothesis

**Status: Confirmed** (statically) for `sqflite` and for
`flutter_inappwebview`'s `WebMessageListener`. The hypothesis explains bugs
1, 3, 4 and 5 fully; bug 2 (mic cue) is independent and real.

Per-plugin platform support, read from each package's own
`pubspec.yaml` `flutter.plugin.platforms` block (pub cache):

| Plugin (version) | Android | Windows | Verdict for this project |
|---|---|---|---|
| `flutter_inappwebview` 6.1.5 (`_windows` 0.6.0) | yes | registered, **but `createPlatformWebMessageListener` is not overridden** | Android only for our use. On Windows `addWebMessageListener` throws `createPlatformWebMessageListener is not implemented on the current platform` (thrown from `flutter_inappwebview_platform_interface-1.3.0+1/lib/src/inappwebview_platform.dart:177`; `grep` finds no override anywhere under `flutter_inappwebview_windows-0.6.0/lib`). This is exactly reported bug 1. |
| `sqflite` 2.4.2+1 | yes (`sqflite_android`) | **no Windows/Linux entry at all** (`android`, `ios`, `macos` only) | Android only. `windows/flutter/generated_plugins.cmake` lists `flutter_inappwebview_windows, flutter_secure_storage_windows, flutter_tts, pdfx, permission_handler_windows, speech_to_text_windows` — **`sqflite` is absent**, so `getDatabasesPath()`/`openDatabase()` throw `MissingPluginException` → Settings save fails (bugs 4, 5). |
| `flutter_secure_storage` 11.2.0 | yes | yes (`_windows`) | cross-platform |
| `speech_to_text` 7.4.0 | yes | yes (`speech_to_text_windows`) | cross-platform in registration; desktop recognizer quality/locales not evaluated — needs device |
| `flutter_tts` 4.2.5 | yes | yes | cross-platform in registration |
| `file_picker` 13.1.0 | yes (`android_file_picker`) | yes (`windows_file_picker`) | cross-platform (explains: the native dialog opened on desktop) |
| `google_mlkit_text_recognition` 0.16.0 | yes | **no** (`android`, `ios` only) | Android/iOS only — OCR fallback is dead on desktop |
| `syncfusion_flutter_pdf` 34.2.8 | pure Dart | pure Dart | cross-platform |
| `pdfx` 2.11.0 | yes | yes | cross-platform |
| `permission_handler` 13.0.2 | yes | yes | **unused**: `grep` finds no `permission_handler` import or `Permission.` in `lib/`. `speech_to_text.initialize()` requests the mic permission itself. Dead dependency (kept because of the `dependency_overrides` pin; not removed here). |

**Default target of `flutter run`.** `flutter devices` on this machine
lists three devices: `Windows (desktop)`, `Chrome (web)`, `Edge (web)` and
no Android device. With more than one device and no `-d`, Flutter prompts
for a choice (or errors when non-interactive) — it does not silently pick
one, so the target depends on what the person chose. The repo has no
Android emulator/AVD config, no CI config, no `launch.json`
(`git ls-files` finds only `.vscode/settings.json`, which is a teammate's
local `cmake.sourceDirectory`). `windows/`, `linux/`, `macos/` and `web/`
runner folders exist in the repo (Flutter scaffolds all platforms by
default), which is what makes a desktop run possible at all. The pubspec has
no platform declarations. Conclusion: a desktop run is entirely plausible
and nothing in the repo prevents or warns about it.

**Fix needed:** yes — startup platform check (Phase 2 item 4). No desktop
support is added.

## 1.2 Stubs, TODOs and mocks leaking into the real path

`grep -rn "UnimplementedError\|TODO\|FIXME" lib/` (excluding `lib/mocks`):

| Hit | On the `USE_MOCK_SERVICES=false` path? |
|---|---|
| `core/constants.dart:4` TODO constrained phrasing | No — a leftover note; prompts already show example phrasing (`narration_lookup.dart`). Comment removed. |
| `core/theme.dart:9` TODO palette | No — `ThemeData()` default. Contrast guideline test passes with it. Deliberate placeholder per `CLAUDE.md`. |
| `services/webview_controller_service.dart:356/364` `focusElement` throws `UnimplementedError` | **Reachable only if called; nothing in the flow calls it.** See below. |

**Status: Confirmed working** (no stub is reachable from the real controller
path).

**`focusElement()` / Feature 2.**
- (a) The spike (milestone 02 / A1b) has **not** been run and no result is
  recorded: `01-intent.md` §4 still says "not yet been confirmed on a real
  device" and §7 lists it as open; `02-spec.md`'s checklist still shows
  A1b unchecked. Status: **Cannot verify without device.**
- (b) Callers: `grep -rn focusElement lib test` → only the fake
  (`lib/mocks`), the service definition, and `spike_harness_screen.dart`
  (which runs its own inline JS, not the service method). The main flow
  never calls it. `application_flow_controller.dart` handles a
  `navigate_to_element` intent by narrating "not available yet" and
  resetting. So Feature 2 is additive, never load-bearing. **Confirmed.**

**Where `useMockServices` is read.** `grep` shows exactly one construction
site: `lib/app.dart` (`WebViewControllerService`, `PdfReaderService`, home
screen `showWebView`, `formPdfPathProvider`, `askUserToChooseFormPdf`) plus
the default in `core/app_config.dart`. There is no service constructed
earlier at another layer. Two notes, neither a leak:
- The default is **`true`**: a plain `flutter run` never touches the real
  site — the mocked flow is what runs unless `--dart-define=USE_MOCK_SERVICES=false`.
- `SpikeHarnessScreen` always builds its own real `WebViewControllerService`
  (debug screen, by design) — which is why bug 3 appeared even in mock mode.

**Fix needed:** no for stubs; yes for the spike harness swallowing errors
(1.8) and the platform check.

## 1.3 OpenAI integration robustness

**Status: Confirmed broken in several ways (all fixed in Phase 2); real
model behaviour Cannot verify without API key.**

`openai_service.dart` (before Phase 2):
- **Markdown fences / prose.** `_completeJson` did a bare `jsonDecode(content)`.
  With `response_format: json_object` the API normally returns bare JSON, but
  a fenced block or leading prose from any model/endpoint change would raise
  and be reported as "unexpected reply shape" — no recovery. Broken →
  fix: strip fences, extract the first balanced JSON object.
- **Key tolerance.** Exact-key lookup only (`json['intentType']`). A
  differently-cased or snake_cased key silently reads as `null`
  (→ `unrecognized` / empty listing). Broken → fix: case- and
  separator-insensitive lookup.
- **Type safety.** Post-processing casts (`json['targetDescription'] as String?`,
  `JobListing.fromJson`'s `as String?`, `reasoning as String?`) run *outside*
  the try/catch that converts errors to `OpenAiException`. A model returning
  a number or list there throws a `TypeError`, which no call site catches
  (they catch `OpenAiException` only) → the flow falls into `start()`'s
  catch-all and ends in `ErrorState` instead of degrading. Broken → fix:
  tolerant getters, and every failure surfaces as `OpenAiException`.
- **Transport errors.** `_client.post` errors other than `TimeoutException`
  (`SocketException`, `http.ClientException`, TLS) propagated raw — same
  "not an `OpenAiException`" problem, and this is the *no network / captive
  wifi at the demo venue* case. Broken → fix.
- **Retry/backoff.** 429 and 5xx: retried twice with linear 1s/2s backoff
  (**Confirmed working**); `Retry-After` was ignored; **timeout was not
  retried at all** (threw immediately). Fix: honour `Retry-After` (capped),
  retry a timeout once.

Call sites (before Phase 2): `_parseIntent`, `_narrateListing`,
`_describeImages`, `_structurePdf`, `_resolveField` catch `OpenAiException`
and fall back to non-AI behaviour — **Confirmed working** for that
exception type. Gap: `submitApplication()` called `ai.matchElement` with no
catch, so an AI outage turned a clearly-best submit candidate into a
failure. Fixed.

Prompt files (`lib/services/prompts/*`): reviewed for fragility — they ask
for a fixed JSON shape, name concrete noise to ignore (listing), and require
`confidence` < 0.7 for ambiguity (matching). Whether the real model obeys
them is **Cannot verify without API key**; the unit tests only prove
parsing/guards against a scripted client.

## 1.4 The two file flows

### (a) Settings CV picker → profile DB

**Status: Confirmed working on Android by trace; Cannot verify without
device end-to-end.**

Trace: `settings_screen.dart` `_pickCv()` → `FilePickerService.pickCvFile()`
→ `setState(_cvFilePath)` → user presses **Save** → `_save()` builds the map
→ `ApplicantProfileService.saveProfile()` → `sqflite` insert + secure-storage
writes. Findings:
- On desktop the failure is the missing `sqflite` Windows plugin (1.1).
  `_save` catches it and shows the "could not save" snackbar, and
  `_load`'s `getProfile` failure is only `Logger.log`ged — the form silently
  shows empty fields. On Android neither should trigger, but the silent
  `_load` catch could still mask a real bug (a corrupt DB) as "no profile
  yet". Fixed: `_load` failure now tells the user.
- **UX gap that also explains bug 5:** picking a file only fills the on-screen
  path; nothing is saved until **Save profile**, and nothing said so. Fixed:
  the pick is announced with an explicit "press Save profile".
- **Android detail — Cannot verify without device:** the saved path is
  whatever `file_picker` returns; on Android that is normally a copy in the
  app's cache directory, which the OS may clear. Since the live form flow no
  longer uses this path (below), the impact is limited to the profile screen
  showing a stale path.

### (b) Live form-fill file upload

**Status: Confirmed broken (design), fixed. Definitive plugin answer below.**

**Definitive answer.** Checked `flutter_inappwebview` **6.1.5** with
`flutter_inappwebview_android` **1.1.3** (`pubspec.lock`). The Android side
implements `WebChromeClient.onShowFileChooser` natively:
`flutter_inappwebview_android-1.1.3/android/src/main/java/com/pichillilorenzo/flutter_inappwebview_android/webview/in_app_webview/InAppWebViewChromeClient.java:836`
→ `startPickerIntent(...)`, with the result returned through
`onActivityResult` (`:842+`). `grep -rn "FileChooser"` over the Dart code of
`flutter_inappwebview_android` and `flutter_inappwebview_platform_interface`
finds **no Dart-level callback** — no `onShowFileChooser` /
`androidOnShowFileChooser` exists in this version. So: **the chooser is fully
automatic; there is nothing to configure or wire**, and milestone 21's
"wire `onShowFileChooser`" instruction cannot be followed as written — the
earlier code comment was right and the milestone spec is wrong. Whether it
actually opens on a device is **Cannot verify without device**.

What *was* broken is our use of it (`_attachCv`, before Phase 2):
1. It called our own `FilePickerService.pickCvFile()` **and then**
   `triggerFileChooser()` — two native pickers back to back, and the path
   from ours is never given to the page (browsers cannot set file inputs).
2. Nothing was said before the page's chooser opened — a blind user lands in
   an unannounced system file picker.
3. It then announced "CV file selected: X" without checking anything was
   attached.

**Open risk — Cannot verify without device, and likely to bite:** the chooser
is opened by JS `input.click()` run through `evaluateJavascript`. Chromium
(and so the Android WebView) generally requires *transient user activation*
to open a file picker; a scripted click with no real tap behind it may be
ignored. If so `triggerFileChooser` still returns `success: true` (the
`click()` ran), no chooser opens, `awaitFileChooser` gives up after 5 s (no
app pause seen) and `getFileInputName` returns nothing — the flow then says
"No CV file was attached, skipping it", i.e. it fails **safe and spoken**, not
silently. A working fallback would be to focus the input and ask the user to
activate it themselves with TalkBack (a real gesture); not built, because it
needs a device to design against.

Fixed: announce first ("your phone's file picker will open; choose your CV
again, then say done"), open only the page's chooser, wait for "done", then
read the input's file name via JS to confirm before narrating success — else
narrate that nothing was attached and skip. The saved profile CV path is not
auto-attached: browser file inputs cannot be set programmatically (already
documented in `02-spec.md` §1), so the user always re-picks at that moment.

## 1.5 CAPTCHA checkpoint end to end

**Status: chain intact; one logic error found and fixed.**

Trace: `dom_reader.js` `__domReader_detectCaptcha` →
`WebViewControllerService.detectCaptcha()` (JS call
`window.__domReader_detectCaptcha()`) →
`CaptchaCheckpointHandler.checkAndHandle` → `tryResolveCaptchaViaAudio()` →
FSM `CaptchaEncountered` → `CaptchaPendingState(interruptedState)` →
controller `_handleCaptcha()` waits for "continue"/"tiếp tục"
(`voice_replies.isContinue`) → `CaptchaResolved` → back to the exact
interrupted state. `narrationFor(CaptchaPendingState)` provides the
on-screen text and `handOffText()` the spoken line, both EN/VI, VI verbatim
from `01-intent.md` §4. No dead link.

- Audio attempt ceiling: `tryResolveCaptchaViaAudio` polls 5 × 400 ms
  (`webview_controller_service.dart`), then returns false — **Confirmed**,
  and a false result goes to the spoken hand-off (not a silent wait).
- **Bug:** when the audio button *was* clicked, the handler narrated "audio
  option used" and returned "handled" — the controller then continued **as if
  the CAPTCHA were solved**. Clicking the audio button only opens the
  challenge; someone still has to listen and type the code. Fixed: the audio
  path now also pauses the FSM and waits for "continue", with narration that
  says to listen and enter the code.
- CAPTCHA is only checked after the initial `readDom()` and again just before
  submit. A CAPTCHA appearing after a field fill (some sites trigger on
  input) would be caught only at submit time. Cannot verify without device
  whether VietnamWorks does that.

## 1.6 Error-handling coverage

**Status: Confirmed broken (two gaps), fixed.**

- (a) Narration: every error is spoken (`narrate(failure(message))`,
  `pageRetrying`, `pdfFailed`, `fillFailed`, `noSuchField`, `fieldNotFound`),
  EN and VI templates. **But** the `message` inside `failure(...)` was a
  hardcoded English literal in 8 places (`"Couldn't reach the AI
  service."`, `'The page did not load.'`, `PdfParseException.message`, …), so
  a Vietnamese user heard a Vietnamese sentence wrapping an English one. The
  submit failure spoke a raw `StateError.toString()`. Fixed: messages come
  from the narration lookup.
- (b) Retry by voice: **none existed.** `RetryRequested` had no caller in
  `lib/` (only the FSM and its tests). Automatic retries exist (page load,
  intent parse, field fill — each retried once through the FSM), but after
  the run ended in `ErrorState` the only recovery was pressing the button,
  which restarted from scratch. Fixed: after an error the app says how to
  retry and listens once; "retry"/"thử lại" resumes (at the final review for
  a failed submit, otherwise a fresh run, at most twice per run).

## 1.7 Accessibility statics

**Status: Confirmed working for what is automated; TalkBack/Scanner Cannot
verify without device.**

- `flutter test test/ui/accessibility_test.dart`: 9/9 pass
  (labeled-tap-target, 48 dp target, text-contrast guidelines on the home and
  settings screens; language options named natively; VI labels).
- Grep of interactive widgets in `lib/ui`: every one has a text label, an
  explicit `Semantics(label:)`, or a `labelText`. Gaps found:
  1. Home screen "Settings" `TextButton` was hardcoded English even with the
     Vietnamese language selected. Fixed (localized).
  2. `MaterialApp.locale` is not set from the language preference
     (`02-spec.md` §7 lists it). Left as a documented gap: making Flutter
     resolve a `vi` locale needs `flutter_localizations` (a new dependency),
     out of scope.
  3. `spike_harness_screen.dart` labels are English-only — debug screen,
     accepted.
- WCAG 1.4.1 (colour not the only cue) applies to the new mic states — see
  the mic UX design below.

## 1.8 Additional real-target problems (not in the brief)

Found by tracing the real path end to end; the first three are fixed, the
rest are recorded because they need a device or a design decision.

| # | Finding | Status | Action |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | No wait-for-stable before `readDom()`. The spec's perceive→act→wait→perceive loop (`02-spec.md` §5) was never implemented: `domChangedEvents` has no listener in the flow, so on an SPA (VietnamWorks) the first read can see a half-rendered page. | Confirmed gap; behaviour Cannot verify without device | Fixed: settle-wait (quiet period, bounded) before each `readDom()` in the flow |
| 2 | `_fields = dom.labeledFields` takes every labeled input on the page — search box, newsletter, login — not just the application form. | Confirmed gap | Fixed (partly): exclude search/submit candidates and non-fillable types |
| 3 | The submit AI-match call was uncaught (1.3). | Confirmed | Fixed |
| 4 | **The flow never reaches the application form.** It loads `AppConfig.targetUrl`, reads that one page, and treats its inputs as the form. Nothing clicks "Apply" and re-reads. Likewise there is no search step (plan: search → read listing → fill form). | Confirmed gap | **Not fixed** — needs a device and a design decision (which button, per-site). Documented as the largest remaining blocker |
| 5 | Real-mode PDF path: the user must pick the form PDF themselves via a native picker (no link from listing to PDF exists yet, `01-intent.md` §7). | Confirmed by design | Documented |
| 6 | `WebMessageListener` registers for one origin only; a redirect to another origin (e.g. a login subdomain) leaves the bridge silent. `readDom` uses `evaluateJavascript` so reading is unaffected; only `domChangedEvents` degrade. | Cannot verify without device | Documented |
| 7 | `addWebMessageListener` needs the WebView's WEB_MESSAGE_LISTENER feature (androidx.webkit) — an old system WebView could throw. | Cannot verify without device | Documented |
| 8 | `flutter_tts.setLanguage('vi-VN')` returns a status we ignore; if the Vietnamese voice pack is missing Android reads Vietnamese text with an English voice. | Cannot verify without device | Documented |
| 9 | `permission_handler` is an unused dependency (1.1). | Confirmed | Documented, not removed |
| 10 | `.env` is bundled as a Flutter asset → a real `OPENAI_API_KEY` is extractable from any shared APK (already accepted in `02-spec.md` §3). | Confirmed, accepted | None |

---

## Mic UX — design chosen before implementing

Problem: `VoiceTriggerButton` shows the same static mic in every state; the
mic is also live during the in-flow confirmations (`listenConfident` in the
per-field loop and final review) while the FSM state is `FillingForm`/
`FinalReview` — so **FSM state alone cannot tell whether the mic is open**,
and a state-driven icon would be wrong exactly when the user is speaking a
field value.

Approach (smallest change, no restructuring of the FSM, `SpeechService` or
the gate's contract): the **`VoiceCommandGate`** is the only place that calls
`speech.listen()`. It gets one narrow signal — an `onListening(bool)`
callback plus start/stop cue hooks — fired immediately around that call.
`ApplicationFlowController` (which owns the gate) republishes it as
`isListening` (it is already a `ChangeNotifier`). The button and the cues
therefore both hang off the same call site and cannot drift.

- Visual: three states with different **icon *and* colour** (WCAG 1.4.1) —
  idle `mic`, listening `hearing`/red, disabled `mic_off`/grey.
- Semantics label changes per state (`narration_lookup.dart`, EN/VI):
  "Start voice command" / "Listening…" / (disabled keeps the base label; the
  `enabled: false` flag conveys it).
- Audio: short spoken cue through the existing `TtsService` (no new plugin;
  Android's `SystemSoundType` offers only one usable sound, so it cannot give
  two distinct cues) — a start cue before `listen()` and, when speech was
  captured, a distinct stop cue. On silence/timeout the existing spoken
  re-prompt is the stop cue.

---

## 2. Phase 2 — what changed

Order followed: 1.2/1.3/1.6/1.7 statics, then 1.4(b), then the mic UX, then
the platform check, then docs. Desktop support was deliberately **not**
added (no `sqflite` Windows plugin, no `WebMessageListener` on Windows).

| Area | Change | Where |
|---|---|---|
| 1.3 OpenAI | Tolerant JSON (strips ```` ``` ```` fences, extracts the first balanced object from prose); case/separator-insensitive keys; wrong-typed fields degrade instead of `TypeError`; **every** failure leaves the service as `OpenAiException` (network, TLS, non-JSON 200, odd shapes); timeout retried once; `Retry-After` honoured (capped 10 s); 429/5xx backoff kept | `services/openai_service.dart`, `test/services/openai_service_robustness_test.dart` |
| 1.3 call sites | `submitApplication` no longer fails when the AI is down and one submit candidate is clearly best | `application_flow_controller.dart` |
| 1.4(a) Settings | Load failure is announced (not just logged); picking a CV says it still needs **Save profile** | `settings_screen.dart` |
| 1.4(b) live upload | Announce first, open **only** the page's chooser (own picker removed), wait for the chooser to close (app lifecycle), read the input's file name via new `__formFiller_getFileName` before claiming success; skip cleanly if nothing attached | `application_flow_controller.dart`, `assets/js/form_filler.js`, `webview_controller_service.dart` (`getFileInputName`), `narration_lookup.dart` |
| 1.5 CAPTCHA | Audio button only *opens* the challenge: the FSM now pauses and waits for "continue" on both the audio and the hand-off path; spoken text follows the language | `captcha_checkpoint_handler.dart` |
| 1.6 errors | All error messages come from the EN/VI lookup (`FlowFailure` carries the localized text through the FSM); voice retry: failed submit resumes at the final review, anything else restarts, max 2, not offered when the microphone itself is unusable | controller, `voice_replies.dart` (`isRetry`) |
| 1.7 a11y | Home "Settings" localized; mic labels EN/VI | `home_screen.dart` |
| 1.8 | Settle-wait before reading the page (`--` real runs only, 800 ms quiet / 8 s cap); unrelated inputs (search box, hidden, buttons, checkboxes, radios) no longer asked about | controller, `app.dart` |
| 1.1 | Non-Android startup screen | `core/platform_support.dart`, `ui/screens/unsupported_platform_screen.dart`, `app.dart` |
| bug 3 | Spike harness shows the load error on screen | `spike_harness_screen.dart` |
| Mic UX | As designed above: `VoiceCommandGate.onListeningChanged` + opt-in `playCues` → `controller.isListening` → button. Three states by icon **and** colour; label "Listening…"/"Đang nghe…". Cues: "Listening"/"Đang nghe" before `listen()`, "Got it"/"Đã nghe rõ" when speech was captured; silence is cued by the spoken re-prompt | gate, controller, `voice_trigger_button.dart` |

Also: removed the stale `TODO` in `core/constants.dart`; removed the unused
`filePicker` dependency from the controller; corrected milestone 21's
`onShowFileChooser` instruction (see `milestone21-*.md`).

Tests added: 196 total now (was 139). New files:
`test/services/openai_service_robustness_test.dart`,
`test/orchestration/audit_fixes_test.dart`,
`test/ui/mic_button_and_platform_test.dart`.

### Not changed, on purpose

- **Windows/Linux/macOS support** (missing `sqflite` Windows plugin,
  `WebMessageListener` on Windows) — out of scope for an Android-first build.
- **Navigation to the application form / search step** (1.8 #4) — needs a
  device and a per-site decision.
- **`permission_handler`** unused dependency — left because of the
  `dependency_overrides` pin.
- **`MaterialApp.locale`** — needs `flutter_localizations`.

---

## 3. Summary — what can and cannot be assumed for a real Android device

**Safe to assume** (verified by static reading and unit/widget tests with
fakes — the logic, not the hardware):
- The OpenAI layer tolerates fenced/prose-wrapped/odd-cased replies, converts
  every failure to `OpenAiException`, retries 429/5xx/timeouts sensibly, and
  every call site degrades to non-AI behaviour.
- The flow's sequencing: gated submit, CAPTCHA pause-until-"continue" (audio or
  hand-off), announce-before-chooser and verify-after, per-field loop with the
  unrelated inputs filtered out, edit loop, voice retry (final review resume /
  fresh run, capped), localized error text.
- The mic button state and the audio cues come from one signal and are
  ordered (mic on → cue → listen → mic off → stop cue); labels/icons differ per
  state in EN and VI.
- Non-Android platforms get an explicit message instead of platform errors.
- 196 tests pass; `flutter analyze` is clean.

**Still needs a device** (not verified, not guessed):
- Real STT (Android often reports no confidence — mapped to 1.0; `vi_VN`
  recognition quality) and real TTS (Vietnamese voice pack; cue audibility and
  whether a spoken cue disturbs recognition).
- `sqflite` + `flutter_secure_storage` persistence and the Settings flow.
- The WebView bridge on a real WebView (`addWebMessageListener` support),
  page-load timeouts, the settle-wait against VietnamWorks, real DOM heuristics.
- The file chooser actually opening from a scripted `click()` (see the risk
  above), `AppLifecycleListener` timing, and the file name read-back.
- CAPTCHA detection and the audio-button selector on the real site.
- TalkBack navigation order and Accessibility Scanner (milestone 43).
- Feature 2 (`focus()` → TalkBack announcement, spike A1b).

**Still needs a live API key:** whether the real models obey the five prompts
(especially the < 0.7 confidence rule for ambiguous fields), intent accuracy
on real EN/VI utterances, vision transcription quality, cost/latency.

**Known gaps, not fixed** (need a device or a design decision): no navigation
from the listing page to the application form and no search step (1.8 #4);
the PDF must be picked by hand on a real run; the flow uses the single
`TARGET_URL` page.
</file>

